{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "קטנתי", :translit "katonti", :gloss "I have become small"} {:he "יו\"ד כפופה", :translit "yud kafufah", :gloss "yud is bent"} {:he "ביו\"ד ברכות", :translit "b'yud berakhot", :gloss "with ten blessings"} {:he "ירא אני שמא יגרום לי החטא", :translit "yare ani she-ma yagormi he-chet", :gloss "I fear lest the sin cause me"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Orthographic observation: the yud in קטנתי is written bent/small."}], :frame {:text "The concept that sin can cause a person to lose the merit of blessings is expressed in the principle that \"the blessing of an ordinary person should not be light in your eyes\" (Megillah 15a). Jacob's statement that he diminished himself alludes to the fact that he had previously received ten blessings from his father Isaac (Genesis 27:27-29). The written form of the word קטנתי visually mirrors its meaning through a bent yud.", :sources ["Megillah 15a" "Genesis 27:27-29"]}} {:quotes [{:he "במקלי", :translit "b'makli", :gloss "with my staff"} {:he "בגימטריא יעקב", :translit "b'gematria ya'akov", :gloss "in gematria Jacob"} {:he "בגופי לבדי", :translit "b'gufi lvadi", :gloss "with my body alone"} {:he "ד\"א בזכות יעקב עברו ישראל את הירדן", :translit "d\"a b'zechut ya'akov avru yisrael et ha-yarden", :gloss "another interpretation: in the merit of Jacob Israel crossed the Jordan"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "במקלי", :b "יעקב"}], :frame {:text "Jacob declares in Genesis 32:11 that he crossed the Jordan 'with my staff.' The gematria equation of במקלי with יעקב supports the reading that Jacob crossed 'with my body alone.' The second interpretation connects Jacob's crossing of the Jordan to Israel's later crossing of the Jordan under Joshua (Joshua 3:14-17), suggesting that Israel merited crossing in the merit of Jacob.", :sources ["Genesis 32:11" "Joshua 3:14-17"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Orthographic observation: the yud in קטנתי is written bent/small.", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :gematria, :a "במקלי", :a-value 182, :b "יעקב", :b-value 182, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? true}], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:09:38.744542315Z", :model "glm-5.2"}